                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><div><strong>Basics of Medical Ergonomics: Digital Motion Tracking and Biomechanical Load Analysis</strong> is a cutting-edge interdisciplinary course integrating medicine and engineering.<br>Breaking through the limitations of traditional qualitative assessments, this course focuses on three modern measurement technologies: force platforms, surface electromyography (sEMG), and inertial measurement unit (IMU) motion capture. Through a combination of theoretical lectures and hands-on practice, students will acquire an in-depth mastery of multimodal sensor data fusion and musculoskeletal system modeling and analysis skills.<br>The course aims to cultivate students' comprehensive research abilities in identifying and analyzing complex ergonomic problems. By utilizing objective digital biomechanical metrics, students will be equipped to accurately assess and provide solutions in the fields of occupational health, clinical rehabilitation, and human-machine interaction.<br>.</div></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
